  "description": "In 2004, LEGO lost almost 2 billion kroner. Why is it booming?\n\nSources:\n- Wikipedia: The Lego Group: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Lego_Group\n- The LEGO Group: record results in 2025 (March 10 2026): https://www.lego.com/en-us/aboutus/news/2026/march/the-lego-group-delivers-record-results-in-2025-driven-by-strong-brand-and-innovative-portfolio\n\nFrom the cited pages: founded 1932 by carpenter Ole Kirk Christiansen; last Lego patent expired 1989; 2003 deficit of DKK 1.4 billion; almost 1,000 employees laid off; 2004 net loss DKK 1,931 million; Kjeld Kirk Kristiansen put DKK 800 million of his private funds into the company in 2004; amusement parks sold; 2025 revenue DKK 83.5 billion (record), net profit DKK 16.7 billion. Not financial advice.\n\n#shorts #lego #business #howtheymakemoney",
